# SOUND — the FIELD-PATH cell of the iterable's SOURCE-PROVENANCE axis.
#
# The ownership tag the fix writes carries a `CollectionId` derived from the
# AST, and that identity is THREE-VALUED: `Some(Local)` for a plain identifier,
# `Some(FieldPath)` for a field chain, and `None` — the degenerate
# `Local(iter_local)` fallback — for anything else. Every other fixture in this
# set iterates a plain local, so the set as prescribed changed three cells of a
# typed axis and pinned one (Core #12: a fixture set that samples one value of a
# typed axis is an anecdote, not a net). This fixture and
# `sound_for_string_elem_source_temp.gg` cover the other two.
#
# Two loops, deliberately: the REBIND loop is what was memory-unsafe (RED at
# HEAD, rc 134), and the ESCAPE loop is what actually READS the tag, so this
# fixture is live against both the view half and the tag half.
#
# PINS the plain-array `set_collection_ref` tag on a non-`Local` source.
# RED-verified against the pre-fix compiler: rc 134 double free; under a revert
# of that tag alone: rc 101 (`UntrackedSourceConsumed`).
struct Bag:
    Vector[String] items

void main():
    Bag b = Bag(Vector[String]())
    b.items.push("aa")
    b.items.push("bb")
    for s in b.items:
        s = "zz"
    Vector[String] out = Vector[String]()
    for s in b.items:
        out.push(s)
    for s in out:
        print(s)
